WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/components/data-display/DataFreshness.tsx — a query-result-driven freshness CHIP (status dot + icon +
  relative-time label) plus the convenience wrapper `DataFreshnessAuto` that derives every chip prop from a
  TanStack Query result (e.g. `useChargingHistory()`). Behaviour reproduced verbatim:
    • Four statuses with precedence `isError ? error : isFetching ? fetching : isStale ? stale : fresh`.
      fresh→Wifi/emerald · fetching→RefreshCw/sky (spins) · stale→Wifi/amber · error→WifiOff/red.
    • Relative-time buckets via `formatRelativeTime`: <60s "just now"; <1h "{{m}}m ago"; <1d "{{h}}h ago";
      <1w "{{d}}d ago"; else "{{w}}w ago" (floor division), re-rendered on a 30s interval.
    • Animations: ping ring while fetching (animate-ping); gentle pulse on background refetch
      (isFetching && updatedAt != null); spinning icon while fetching — all gated by Reduce Motion.
    • Tooltip (`title`): "Updating…" / "Last updated: {{time}}" / "Never updated".
    • a11y: role=button when refetchable (label "Refresh"), else role=status ("Data freshness: {{state}}"),
      aria-live=polite + aria-atomic=true; stable-width tabular-nums label.
    • Props: `compact` (icon-only) · `refetchable` · `forceStaleAfterMs` (Auto wrapper).
  Data sources (prompt): useQuery · useTranslation · useMotionPreference · useDateFormat · useChargingHistory —
  bound here through the shared P1/S8 state-holder seam (no HTTP in the view).

